V='VI. Additional hypothesis and notation checks'
add('Unequal reducible components test the claimed automorphism quotient','033,035','033:37–40; 035:23–33','own idea',r'''For $R=\{\pm e_1,\pm\sqrt2e_2\}$ the globally normalized Dynkin graph has two isolated vertices labeled1 and2, hence no nontrivial labeled-graph automorphism. Yet the linear map exchanging $e_1$ with $\sqrt2e_2$ preserves $R$ and survives modulo the Weyl group of independent sign changes. Thus the visible $\mathrm{GL}(V)$-defined $A(R)/W(R)$ has a component swap that the globally labeled graph omits. This tests the reducible scope of the corollary, independently of the valid single-rescaling step under matching global labels.''',TCTX+' No automorphism-quotient or unequal-A1-component example occurs; adds a separate literal-scope test.',TREG,['A(R)','Weyl','automorphism','Dynkin','reducible'],'High under the visible global labels and GL definition; an inherited irreducibility convention would exclude this example.',source='Own two-component linear calculation, independently reviewed in records/reused_formula_qa.md.',section=V)
add('The cohomology-of-functor shorthand is naturally restricted to degree-zero inputs','042','9–12','reading question',r'''The input-free identity $\mathcal H^i(R_!f_*)=R^i_!f_*$ naturally recovers the earlier cohomological functor on sheaves placed in degree zero. It should not be used to identify hypercohomology on an arbitrary complex with a higher direct image of one term or one cohomology sheaf. This is a suppressed convention to recover, not evidence that the displayed derived functor is wrongly constructed.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md, N11, scan112, and N33, scans138–142: adds another literal shorthand whose type-complete interpretation matters; no same formula is supplied.','MPL_33_098-146 N08 and §76.',['hypercohomology','shorthand','complex','cohomology sheaves'],source='The Stacks Project Authors (n.d.), Lemma 13.21.3, Tag 015J, for the general complex comparison.',section=V)
add('The deduction of Artin finiteness is asserted with inherited hypotheses','048','2–10,20–22','unproved claim',r'''“On retrouve le th. de finitude de Artin” suppresses the passage from compact-support finiteness through duality and the required smoothness, coefficient and constructibility assumptions. In particular, the positive finite-local-system comparison in N48 does not establish an unrestricted theorem for arbitrary locally constant modules. The subsequent change from “finitude” to the doubtful “constructiblt.|constructibilité” is consequential for the partial-range proposal in N49–N50.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md, N19, scans112/120, and N30, scans136/140/142: adds a compressed finiteness deduction distinct from their global finite-Tor requirement; no exact partial-range result is supplied.','MPL_33_098-146 N30 and §76; no status change.',['finitude','finiteness','constructib','duality','Artin'],source='Deligne (1973), SGA 4 XVIII, §3.2.6: finite locally constant coefficients in the checked comparison.',section=V)
add('Relative purity over an arbitrary base is a distinct announcement','014','36–37','unproved claim',r'''“Il y a aussi un th de pureté relatif sur une base quelconque” follows the absolute regularity problem, but no complete relative hypotheses or formula are supplied at this locus. Smooth pairs over a common base give one precise comparison setting; replacing the base by an arbitrary scheme does not mean that all immersions over it become pure. The relative announcement therefore deserves its own reconstruction rather than being absorbed into the later absolute-purity theorem.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md: no same relative-purity statement; N01, scan098, concerns a later duality exchange and N20, scan122, a resolution-free curve expectation. Adds a distinct geometric hypothesis question.','MPL_33_098-146 N01 and §76; no settled same-point result.',['relative purity','pureté','smooth pair','arbitrary base','duality'],source='Artin (1973c), SGA 4 XVI, Theorem 3.7, for smooth pairs; comparison scope only.',section=V)
add('The E7 and E8 order descriptions require their missing convention','031,049','031:25–35,41–45; 049:7','reading question',r'''The E7 discussion uses an order induced by the “ordre lexicographique,” whereas the E8 highest-root paragraph specifies the opposite lexicographic order. Without the missing definition in the reused source’s no.10, one cannot decide whether this is shorthand, a convention change, or a source error. The orthogonality argument selecting the E7 subsystem does not by itself choose the intended positive ordering.''',TCTX+' No lexicographic-order convention is supplied; adds a distinct collation question.',TREG,['lexicographic','lexicographique','positive','E7','E8'],section=V)
add('The surviving shriek in the relative-duality explanation is substantive','048','14–18','reading question',r'''The explanatory line retains $R^{-i}_!f_*(DF)$ while the adjoining duality displays cancel the shriek on the corresponding direct image. Consequently its local-constancy claim cannot simply be described as the immediate consequence of the ordinary-direct-image isomorphism written beside it. This may reflect a source slip or additional inherited hypotheses, but the research notes do not erase the support distinction.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md, N18, scan120, and N30, scans136/140/142: adds a new literal support mismatch; those leads distinguish ordinary and compact-support operations without deciding this ink.','MPL_33_098-146 N30 and §76.',['shriek','compact-support','ordinary','support','local constancy'],section=V)
add('The Kummer image-zero observation has a degree-two global-preimage condition','028','21–23','unproved claim',r'''The NB begins with a doubtful “si” and a global $\beta\in H^1_Y(X,G_m)$, then applies the Kummer boundary into $H^2_Y(X,\mu_n)$. Exactness makes that boundary class map to zero in $H^2_Y(X,G_m)$. This is a conditional degree-two statement, separate from the arbitrary-codimension degree-$2d$ edge construction above it, and it does not assert such a global $G_m$ preimage for every local fundamental class.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md: no Kummer/global-preimage point occurs; N01, scan098, supplies only a thematic support/duality parallel. Adds a specific low-degree qualification.','MPL_33_098-146 N01 and §76 at the programme level.',['Kummer','G_m','boundary','supported','degree-two'],section=V)
add('The point-class normalization distinguishes rational from arbitrary closed points','028,030','028:25–38; 030:2–8','own idea',r'''The edited point wording matters over a separably closed imperfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$: choose $a\notin k^p$ and the closed point $x\subset\mathbb A^1_k$ cut out by $T^p-a$, which has degree $p$. Its divisor-class trace is $p$, whereas a $k$-rational point has trace1; with coefficients $\mathbb Z/(p+1)$ these values differ and both are units. Thus a basis assertion can survive while independence from every closed point fails. This tests only the stronger unrestricted-point reading and supports recovering the rational-point convention suggested by the doubtful cancelled insertion “pt sur $k$”.''','same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md: no same inseparable-point degree example occurs; N14, scans118–120, uses a separably closed base in a different Künneth statement, and N29/N37, scans134–136/146, concern different trace constructions. Adds a new point-normalization scope test.','MPL_33_098-146 N29 and N37 at the geometric-trace comparison level; no prior result is re-derived.',['rational','inseparable','degree','point','trace'],'High for the degree calculation and its conditional application; the edited source does not securely specify the live point convention.',source='Deligne (1973), SGA 4 XVIII, §1.1.6 and Theorem 2.9, for degree normalization; the imperfect-field example is our own.',section=V)

def search_items(items):
    files=[CTX/'README.md',CTX/'notes/RESULTS_STATE.md',CTX/'same_cote_33/MPL_33_098-146_notes.md']
    out=[]
    for x in items:
        fs=[]
        for p in files:
            cmd=['rg','-n','-i','-F']
            for q in x['queries']: cmd+=['-e',q]
            z=subprocess.run(cmd+[str(p)],text=True,capture_output=True)
            if z.returncode not in (0,1): raise RuntimeError(z.stderr)
            fs.append({'file':str(p.relative_to(CTX)),'queries':x['queries'],'match_count':len(z.stdout.splitlines()),'matching_lines':z.stdout.splitlines()})
        out.append({'id':x['id'],'files_searched':fs,'substantive_disposition':x['context']})
    return out

def main():
    for x in ITEMS:
        if x['kind']=='own idea' and not x.get('confidence'): raise ValueError(x['id'])
    aux_terms={
      'T01':['reused','foreground','49 scans','scope'],
      'T02':['title','dualité globale','compactifiable','heading'],
      'T03':['foliation','page total','pagination','handwritten'],
      'T04':['Formulaire','heading','number','section'],
      'T05':['391','Bourbaki','pagination','reused'],
      'T06':['plate','root','Dynkin','type'],
      'T07':['Tribu','Variétés de groupe','formal','page'],
      'T08':['Gray','sheafification','English','printed'],
      'T09':['19.6','1007','EGA','filtré','cancelled'],
    }
    tail=(ROOT/'records/notes_backmatter.md').read_text()
    aux=[]
    for match in re.finditer(r'^### (T\d+)\. (.*?)\n(.*?)(?=^### T|^## IX\.|\Z)',tail,re.M|re.S):
        ident,title,body=match.groups()
        context=re.search(r'\*\*Context:\*\* (.*)',body)
        aux.append({'id':ident,'title':title,'context':context.group(1) if context else 'See title inventory.','queries':aux_terms[ident]})
    if len(aux)!=9: raise ValueError(f'Expected9 title items, found {len(aux)}')
    ledger=search_items(ITEMS+aux)
    (ROOT/'records/research_items.json').write_text(json.dumps(ITEMS,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
    (ROOT/'records/research_context_searches.json').write_text(json.dumps(ledger,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
    intro=(ROOT/'records/notes_frontmatter.md').read_text()
    out=[intro.rstrip()+'\n']
    section=None
    for x in ITEMS:
        if x['section']!=section:
            section=x['section'];out.append(f'\n## {section}\n')
        out.append(f"\n### {x['id']}. {x['title']}\n\n**File:** cote 33. **Scan(s):** {x['scans']}. **Frozen page-file line(s):** {x['lines']}. **Kind:** {x['kind']}.\n\n{x['body']}\n")
        if x.get('confidence'):out.append(f"\n**Confidence and reason:** {x['confidence']}\n")
        out.append(f"\n**Context search and relationship:** {x['context']}\n\n**Results register:** {x['register']}\n")
        if x.get('source'):out.append(f"\n**Primary comparison / verification:** {x['source']}\n")
    out.append('\n'+tail.strip()+'\n')
    notes='\n'.join(out)
    # Research prose typography only; protect URLs, code and mathematics.
    # This formatter is never applied to a diplomatic file.
    words='scan scans cote cotes folios folio page pages Theorem Corollary Lemma Proposition Exposé exposé Tome Chapter Chapitres reference section version published July November on in by and at onto except note sheet chiefly title conditions denominator order ratio squared proposition labeled trace across within lines doubtful giving has present sections carries initial before circled outlines develops separate example these the enumerates plates while numbers handwritten neither nor complete including locator et all'.split()+['Fujiwara’s']
    def prose_spacing(s):
        s=re.sub(r'\b('+ '|'.join(re.escape(w) for w in words) +r')(?=\d)',r'\1 ',s,flags=re.I)
        s=re.sub(r'\b(section|chapter|exposé|plates)(?=[IVX]+\b)',r'\1 ',s,flags=re.I)
        s=re.sub(r'\b(XI|XV|XVI|XVIII)(?=\d)',r'\1 ',s)
        s=s.replace('SGA4','SGA 4').replace('SGA1962','SGA 1962').replace('Hartshorne1961','Hartshorne 1961')
        s=re.sub(r'\b(pp?\.|Vol\.|Nos\.|no\.)\s*(?=\d)',r'\1 ',s)
        return re.sub(r'(?<=\d),(?=\d{4}\b)',', ',s)
    segments=re.split(r'(https?://[^\s)]+|`[^`\n]+`|\$[^$\n]*\$)',notes)
    notes=''.join(part if i%2 else prose_spacing(part) for i,part in enumerate(segments))
    (ROOT/'MPL_33_002-049_notes.md').write_text(notes)
    print(f'Wrote {len(ITEMS)} research items; {len(ledger)*3} file searches; {len(notes.split())} words.')
    print('\n'.join(f"{x['id']} {x['title']}" for x in ITEMS[36:]))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
